# Build-context hygiene (issues 084/069): images only COPY pyproject.toml,
# README.md, requirements.lock (slim) and voyage/ — tests/ are bind-mounted
# at gate time, never baked in (issue 054). Everything below just inflates
# the transferred context (output/ alone is ~400 MB of frames/videos) and
# churns the layer cache on every render. Keep COPY sources unlisted here.
output/
.git
*_cache/
# Explicit dot-cache trio (069): the `*_cache/` glob above does match them
# under Go filepath.Match semantics, but explicit entries survive builder
# changes and document what the gates actually write into the tree.
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Gate/dev residue (069, mirrors .gitignore issue 085): coverage embeds
# absolute paths and must never leak into build layers.
.coverage
coverage.xml
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.env
# Stray run artifacts at the Voyage root (mirrors .gitignore): a
# misdirected --output or local probe must never inflate the build
# context or churn the layer cache, esp. multi-hundred-MB media.
*.mp4
*.wav
*.flac
*.pt
*.log
issues/
reports/
